WEBVTT

00:03.090 --> 00:06.480
I hate this place. It's swarming with bugs.

00:06.760 --> 00:11.290
A-Are you sure we're ready 
to fight the area boss?

00:11.290 --> 00:13.360
What's gotten you so scared all of a sudden?

00:13.610 --> 00:16.590
We've beaten everything 
they've thrown at us so far!

00:16.590 --> 00:18.170
But...

00:19.370 --> 00:21.370
We can take this, no pro—

00:22.920 --> 00:24.870
What the heck's this?

00:25.690 --> 00:27.440
I can't get it off! It's too sticky!

00:27.440 --> 00:28.530
Are you okay?

00:30.810 --> 00:32.570
S-Soma.

00:33.040 --> 00:33.790
Is that...

00:39.270 --> 00:43.560
A clown?!

00:47.890 --> 00:51.690
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:52.940 --> 00:57.180
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:58.570 --> 01:01.350
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

01:01.350 --> 01:06.640
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

01:06.640 --> 01:11.270
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

01:12.960 --> 01:16.830
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

01:16.830 --> 01:20.070
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

01:20.890 --> 01:25.620
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:57.380 --> 03:03.010
<b>Let's Go Tomb Raiding!!</b>

03:01.180 --> 03:04.970
The area boss here is a spider, right?

03:05.340 --> 03:06.470
Yes, indeed!

03:06.470 --> 03:08.120
It's called the Clown Spider!

03:08.120 --> 03:11.400
So... we're probably getting close.

03:18.410 --> 03:19.390
Okay!

03:21.100 --> 03:23.410
Huh? I can't go in?

03:23.070 --> 03:24.640
Other players are
fighting this area boss.

03:24.640 --> 03:27.840
It appears other pioneers 
have already engaged it!

03:36.760 --> 03:39.470
Damn it! I gotta climb all 
the way back up there?

03:39.470 --> 03:41.570
This boss is such a pain in the ass.

03:41.570 --> 03:45.030
This isn't over! One good hit and I'm—

03:46.490 --> 03:50.680
It flattened that pioneer!

03:49.660 --> 03:51.250
Rest in peace.

03:55.700 --> 03:57.430
Welp, path's open. Let's go!

03:57.430 --> 03:59.320
You didn't mourn him for long!

03:59.320 --> 04:03.050
{M}He's just respawning in Thirdrema. Chill out.

04:06.110 --> 04:09.490
But thanks to Mr. Pancake there, 
I got some useful info.

04:24.010 --> 04:25.280
Emul.

04:25.280 --> 04:28.460
You mind hanging out here 
and doing color commentary?

04:29.880 --> 04:32.400
I wanna solo the Clown Spider

04:32.400 --> 04:35.330
on my first try, with a no-damage run.

04:37.130 --> 04:39.630
And you really want me 
to stay here and watch?

04:41.060 --> 04:42.010
Yeah.

04:42.400 --> 04:45.010
Okay! Let's do this, area boss!

04:51.360 --> 04:52.760
I'm fighting a spider.

04:53.210 --> 04:56.850
The webbing's gonna get 
denser the higher I get.

04:56.850 --> 05:00.420
Out of the skills I learned 
leveling up in the arena...

04:59.960 --> 05:03.860
Rush Slash
Quick Spin
Loop Slash Lv. 5
 Accel Lv. 6
 One-Boat Leap

05:01.020 --> 05:03.860
I think my best bet here'll be...

05:07.490 --> 05:08.250
Skill...

05:09.600 --> 05:11.100
One-Boat Leap!

05:10.430 --> 05:12.370
<b>One-Boat Leap</b>

05:15.000 --> 05:16.880
Bet you use that to insta-kill first-timers.

05:16.880 --> 05:19.370
Good thing I saw you use it already.

05:27.890 --> 05:30.280
Sunraku-san! You're heading right for...

05:35.400 --> 05:37.100
a sticky web!

05:38.940 --> 05:41.070
It wasn't sticky?!

05:41.070 --> 05:44.820
The radial threads of a 
spider's web aren't sticky.

05:45.260 --> 05:48.770
That makes it a little harder 
to get stable footing.

05:48.770 --> 05:50.500
But if I judge it just right...

05:52.660 --> 05:54.830
Skill, Accel Lv. 6!

05:56.540 --> 05:59.290
It's not too different from 
running around that forest!

06:04.670 --> 06:06.760
I-Incredible!

06:10.420 --> 06:15.230
The time for sitting back and throwing 
stuff is over, Clown Spider.

06:16.060 --> 06:19.190
<b>Area Boss
Clown Spider</b>

06:29.200 --> 06:33.080
Loop Slash!

06:33.080 --> 06:34.580
<b><i>Loop Slash</i></b>

06:34.810 --> 06:36.410
Right leg down!

06:40.120 --> 06:42.300
Rush Slash!

06:54.160 --> 06:57.200
A fall from that height should 
dish out some juicy damage.

06:59.310 --> 07:00.840
Not a damn chance!

06:59.810 --> 07:01.150
<b>Throwing Knife
</b>equipped.

07:13.620 --> 07:16.620
Th-That looked quite painful!

07:17.300 --> 07:20.890
Probably won't be enough to beat it, but...

07:26.400 --> 07:29.960
Well, lookie there!

07:48.720 --> 07:51.280
Aiming's a breeze against a target that big!

07:51.640 --> 07:55.030
I really got you in a tough spot, huh?

07:55.030 --> 07:59.050
Oh, you're brilliant, Sunraku-san!

07:59.050 --> 08:02.300
You can easily make it 
through unharmed like this!

08:02.300 --> 08:04.080
There we go.

08:08.320 --> 08:12.670
Well, that's all fun enough, but...

08:15.470 --> 08:16.640
Sunraku-san?

08:19.100 --> 08:20.220
Hup!

08:24.140 --> 08:28.400
If I can't beat an area boss head-to-head...

08:49.830 --> 08:51.210
I'll never make it

08:51.630 --> 08:54.450
to Lycagon's level!

09:11.900 --> 09:13.740
<b></b>Area Boss
<b>Clown Spider</b>

09:12.360 --> 09:13.740
<b>Dispatch Complete</b>

09:13.740 --> 09:15.850
Sunraku-san!

09:16.330 --> 09:17.750
Well, Emul?

09:18.870 --> 09:22.360
I called it. First-time, no-damage run.

09:22.360 --> 09:24.120
Yes indeed!

09:24.120 --> 09:26.570
You're a true man of your word!

09:27.450 --> 09:29.690
Felt almost too easy.

09:29.690 --> 09:31.960
It went right to his head!

09:35.090 --> 09:38.040
Hey, an email from Pencil Knight.

09:37.900 --> 09:41.140
Let's get up to some mischief!

From: Pencil Knight
 To: Modor Katzo

09:39.080 --> 09:41.140
Oh, it's about that.

09:43.480 --> 09:48.920
I thought Sunraku picking this game 
up would be a good reason to try it...

09:53.450 --> 09:57.590
But soloing these bosses isn't the 
challenge they made it out to be...

10:01.070 --> 10:04.950
I hope what you've got in 
store has a little more bite.

10:02.700 --> 10:08.080
<b><i>Oikatzo</i></b>

10:14.590 --> 10:16.590
<b>Major Summer Update!!</b>

10:14.590 --> 10:16.590
<b>The Severed Sea</b>

10:14.590 --> 10:16.590
<b>The Frontier Fleet</b>

10:14.590 --> 10:16.590
<b>The New Land</b>

10:18.060 --> 10:21.010
Hey, he accepted your friend request?

10:21.010 --> 10:21.890
That's so great!

10:22.240 --> 10:23.440
Y-Yes.

10:23.440 --> 10:26.390
I worked up my nerve, and he accepted it.

10:26.730 --> 10:29.530
I couldn't have done it 
without your encouragement.

10:30.790 --> 10:33.700
But Hizutome-kun really is amazing!

10:33.700 --> 10:36.400
Not only did he skip the first town,

10:36.400 --> 10:39.430
he's got a Vorpal Bunny companion!
We all thought you couldn't tame those!

10:39.430 --> 10:42.990
Wow. Well, that's a trash gamer for you.

10:46.220 --> 10:47.880
Welcome!

10:56.980 --> 10:59.130
He hasn't been here for a few days.

10:59.130 --> 11:01.160
Guess he's been in <i>SLF</i> the whole time?

11:01.160 --> 11:03.050
He's a real wild card, though.

11:03.050 --> 11:06.260
He might even be the first 
to dispatch a unique monster!

11:08.150 --> 11:10.320
Oh, not even he could do that!

11:13.000 --> 11:15.210
<i>Actually, maybe he could!</i>

11:44.280 --> 11:47.010
Hey, an interview with Katzo.

11:47.010 --> 11:54.230
<b>Kei Uomi
</b>Pro Gamer

11:48.090 --> 11:50.950
That guy talks so much shit.

11:50.950 --> 11:54.230
I bet he made the editor's job hell.

11:56.490 --> 11:59.500
<i>SLF</i>'s getting a major summer update?

12:00.010 --> 12:02.020
The Severed Sea.

12:02.020 --> 12:03.390
The Frontier Fleet.

12:03.850 --> 12:06.870
The New Land, and a new job...

12:07.510 --> 12:11.710
I guess this is the one Pencilgon 
was talking about yesterday.

12:13.320 --> 12:15.040
Hello, hello!

12:15.040 --> 12:17.210
Thank you both for coming today.

12:17.210 --> 12:22.470
Pencil Knight

12:17.570 --> 12:22.470
When was the last time we were all 
together here in <i>Unite Rounds</i>?

12:22.990 --> 12:30.180
Was it when you jackasses stormed my castle, 
which had an eighty-player garrison?

12:30.180 --> 12:42.570
Sunraku

12:30.180 --> 12:42.570
Pencil Knight

12:30.180 --> 12:42.570
Katzo Tataki

12:30.480 --> 12:33.820
Look, that was Sunraku's idea.

12:33.820 --> 12:36.860
"Assassinating the monarch 
sounds like a blast!" he said.

12:36.860 --> 12:38.860
You were just as down for it!

12:38.860 --> 12:40.480
Hell yeah, I was.

12:40.480 --> 12:42.570
And it freaking ruled!

12:42.570 --> 12:45.250
Yeah, I wasn't expecting it to end with her

12:45.250 --> 12:49.310
blowing up the castle and 
all her retainers with it!

12:50.230 --> 12:52.410
Yeah, the Pencil Dynasty Incident.

12:52.410 --> 12:56.540
They'll be talking about that one 'til 
the <i>Unite Rounds</i> servers shut down!

12:56.540 --> 12:57.850
Yeah.

12:57.850 --> 13:01.360
And she acts like it was just part 
of her "live in the moment" attitude,

13:01.360 --> 13:03.840
but you can tell she's 
still so pissed about it!

13:03.840 --> 13:07.580
She'll start making excuses even 
when no one's brought it up—

13:08.560 --> 13:11.580
Now that we're all feeling nice and relaxed,

13:11.930 --> 13:14.310
do you mind if I get to the main topic?

13:14.310 --> 13:15.210
Yes, ma'am!

13:17.130 --> 13:18.260
Good.

13:18.860 --> 13:24.910
I'm betting you called us here to say 
more than just "Let's play <i>SLF</i> together."

13:27.390 --> 13:28.430
That's right.

13:28.790 --> 13:30.540
We don't have a lot of time,

13:30.540 --> 13:32.410
so I'll get right to the point.

13:34.250 --> 13:38.650
Want to take out the unique monster, 
Wethermon the Tombguard,

13:38.650 --> 13:40.130
with just the three of us?

13:47.380 --> 13:50.890
Huh?! A unique monster?!

13:51.450 --> 13:53.020
A unique monster...

13:53.020 --> 13:57.050
That's the same category of monster as 
that Lycagon thing Sunraku fought, right?!

13:57.050 --> 13:58.480
Are you for real?!

13:58.480 --> 14:01.360
I'm dying to fight those unique guys!

14:01.360 --> 14:02.790
That's right.

14:02.790 --> 14:07.370
One of the Seven Colossi 
of <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>...

14:08.470 --> 14:10.370
Wethermon the Tombguard.

14:10.370 --> 14:12.170
<i>Hold on a minute.</i>

14:12.170 --> 14:16.370
<i>I figured she'd be inviting us on 
some high-level clan raid, but...</i>

14:19.780 --> 14:21.880
You said "just the three of us"?

14:21.880 --> 14:22.750
Yes.

14:23.790 --> 14:26.020
And you think we stand a chance?

14:26.020 --> 14:29.380
I don't know jack about 
this "Wethermon" thing.

14:29.740 --> 14:33.370
Well, it's not like you can beat 
him with sheer force of numbers.

14:33.370 --> 14:38.830
We went at him with Ashura Kai's 
fifteen best and got wasted.

14:38.830 --> 14:40.550
Is this the kind of monster that gets

14:40.550 --> 14:43.480
more attack and HP the more 
people you send at it?

14:43.480 --> 14:45.150
That's part of it, but...

14:46.400 --> 14:50.010
I can't tell you more until 
I have your agreement.

14:52.170 --> 14:53.920
We get one chance at this.

14:54.240 --> 14:56.240
We'll carry it out in two weeks.

14:56.240 --> 14:59.880
The night of the new moon, 
right after the major summer update.

15:01.120 --> 15:02.790
That's the day we'll do it.

15:06.760 --> 15:07.980
What do you think?

15:09.230 --> 15:11.000
<i>Right after the update?</i>

15:11.000 --> 15:14.750
<i>Why invite a pair of </i>SLF<i> newbies, though?</i>

15:14.750 --> 15:19.290
<i>Wouldn't she want a few max-level elites?</i>

15:19.290 --> 15:23.310
If you're worried about your levels, 
that won't be a problem.

15:24.310 --> 15:28.180
What I'm after is pure player skill.

15:29.220 --> 15:30.510
That's why I'm enlisting

15:30.820 --> 15:33.310
Katzo-kun, the pro gamer,

15:33.310 --> 15:36.900
and Sunraku-kun, the trash gamer.

15:41.330 --> 15:45.340
<b>Pencil Knight</b>

15:45.340 --> 15:49.880
<b>Sunraku</b>

15:45.340 --> 15:49.880
<b>Katzo Tataki</b>

15:47.570 --> 15:50.750
You sure those two things are comparable?

15:50.750 --> 15:52.740
Feel free to back off, trash gamer.

15:52.740 --> 15:54.410
You're stinking up my pro gamer rep.

15:54.410 --> 15:56.160
What was that?!

15:56.160 --> 15:57.620
So, what do you think?

15:58.040 --> 16:00.350
I can always offer additional compensation.

16:01.370 --> 16:04.350
Well... I think I might be down.

16:04.870 --> 16:07.850
But I also think you're 
still hiding something.

16:08.360 --> 16:13.890
If you want us to buy in, 
you'd better give us the full story.

16:19.120 --> 16:20.420
All right.

16:20.420 --> 16:22.650
Shall we begin our strategy meeting?

16:24.620 --> 16:27.500
<b>Weekly</b>

16:24.620 --> 16:27.500
VR Full Diver

16:24.620 --> 16:27.500
<b>Comes with 
B3 Poster
of the cover page</b>

16:27.510 --> 16:29.500
Thank you for coming!

16:33.460 --> 16:34.890
E-Excuse me!

16:40.580 --> 16:42.680
H-Hizutome-kun...

16:42.900 --> 16:44.930
H-Hello!

16:47.690 --> 16:50.620
<i>Hey, isn't she...</i>

16:50.620 --> 16:54.480
<i>Pretty sure she was in my class last year...</i>

16:54.480 --> 16:55.840
<i>Um...</i>

16:56.880 --> 16:59.400
<i>Ga... Ga-san...</i>

16:59.400 --> 17:00.990
<i>Her name, her name...</i>

17:00.990 --> 17:02.170
<i>It was something-ga-san!</i>

17:05.660 --> 17:06.860
<i>Just hold on.</i>

17:06.860 --> 17:08.200
<i>Rack your brain, man.</i>

17:10.870 --> 17:12.630
<i>Iga? Koga?</i>

17:13.840 --> 17:15.000
That's it!

17:15.000 --> 17:16.410
You're Saiga-san!

17:16.860 --> 17:18.940
Y-Yes, that's right!

17:18.940 --> 17:20.500
I'm Rei Saiga!

17:20.500 --> 17:21.810
Hell yeah!

17:21.810 --> 17:24.630
I-Isn't it funny that 
we ran into each other?!

17:24.630 --> 17:26.170
Yeah, sure is.

17:26.990 --> 17:29.260
W-Were you shopping?

17:29.260 --> 17:30.690
Y-Yeah...

17:30.690 --> 17:31.730
What about you?

17:31.730 --> 17:34.060
I'm on my way to practice...

17:31.730 --> 17:39.990
<b>Judo</b>

17:34.060 --> 17:34.970
Practice?

17:34.970 --> 17:36.110
Judo—

17:36.110 --> 17:40.380
Er, I mean... well...

17:40.380 --> 17:44.150
Oh, Mana-san from Rock Roll told me...

17:44.150 --> 17:46.910
You started playing <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>?

17:46.910 --> 17:49.060
Oh, yeah.

17:49.060 --> 17:50.040
I'm playing.

17:50.040 --> 17:54.690
So... er... I...

17:55.170 --> 17:59.210
I also play... <i>SLF</i>, so...

17:59.800 --> 18:01.280
Oh?

18:01.280 --> 18:04.300
<i>It even gets girls from 
rich old families playing?</i>

18:04.300 --> 18:05.810
<i>SLF</i>'s really something.

18:05.810 --> 18:10.500
D-Do you think... w-we could play...?

18:10.910 --> 18:12.750
Oh, sorry. Got an email.

18:12.750 --> 18:13.690
Hang on.

18:13.690 --> 18:16.690
R-Right! G-Go ahead!

18:21.700 --> 18:25.700
From: Pencil Knight
To: Sunraku
Get over here
 Are you dying of remorse over keeping me waiting?
Are you okay? Should I call an ambulance?

18:22.330 --> 18:23.320
"Get over here"?

18:23.940 --> 18:25.700
Yeah, figured it'd be Pencilgon.

18:25.970 --> 18:28.480
Can't I even buy groceries in peace?

18:29.520 --> 18:32.880
And she's double emailing! Scary...

18:33.290 --> 18:34.560
Sorry, Saiga-san!

18:34.560 --> 18:36.500
I've got a friend who won't wait.

18:36.500 --> 18:37.300
Gotta go!

18:38.190 --> 18:39.610
See you later!

18:39.610 --> 18:41.090
O-Of course!

18:41.600 --> 18:43.770
I'm so sorry I kept you!

18:49.140 --> 18:51.270
That was so exciting!

18:51.270 --> 18:53.900
We talked so much!

18:55.140 --> 18:56.920
But Hizutome-kun...

18:56.920 --> 18:59.720
He had so many energy drinks.

19:00.370 --> 19:03.870
I suppose he'll be playing <i>SLF</i> for a while...

19:07.820 --> 19:10.540
Maybe I'll get to see him soon!

19:15.050 --> 19:17.320
Oh, I've got to get to practice!

19:25.560 --> 19:30.310
Shoot. I should've asked Saiga-san's handle.

19:32.100 --> 19:34.550
Welcome to <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>.

19:38.350 --> 19:40.740
Good morning, Sunraku-san!

19:43.330 --> 19:45.190
Emul. Back off.

19:45.190 --> 19:46.450
Righty-o!

19:46.940 --> 19:49.610
Well? What's on the agenda today!

19:53.370 --> 19:56.040
First, I've got a question for you.

19:56.040 --> 19:57.370
What is it?

19:58.090 --> 20:00.130
It looks like, in two weeks,

20:00.570 --> 20:04.260
I'll be picking a fight with 
"Wethermon the Tombguard."

20:04.570 --> 20:08.810
It's looking like I'll have to leave 
you out of the party while I do...

20:09.490 --> 20:10.290
What's wrong?

20:10.290 --> 20:15.020
Picking a fight with <i>Wethermon</i>?!

20:16.770 --> 20:20.910
D-Da... Bo...

20:20.910 --> 20:23.880
Daboo... Bodadd...

20:23.880 --> 20:28.790
I've got to tell my daddy!

20:27.170 --> 20:28.260
Hey!

20:30.100 --> 20:31.530
What's her problem?

20:31.530 --> 20:34.730
I'm late to see Pencilgon as it is!

20:37.450 --> 20:38.540
Here's a question.

20:39.450 --> 20:40.430
What is it?

20:40.820 --> 20:43.500
You said "just the three of us,"

20:43.980 --> 20:47.080
but I've got an NPC in my party right now.

20:47.580 --> 20:48.560
What about her?

20:49.080 --> 20:51.850
Oh, the infamous bunny.

20:51.850 --> 20:53.370
Bunny?

20:53.370 --> 20:56.520
If you care about her, 
you should keep her out of it.

20:57.840 --> 20:59.380
What's with the bunny?

20:59.380 --> 21:00.780
What do you mean?

21:01.250 --> 21:02.820
In <i>SLF</i>...

21:02.820 --> 21:04.850
Oh, dear! Oh, dear!

21:04.850 --> 21:06.570
Once an NPC dies...

21:06.970 --> 21:09.050
It's truly terrible!

21:09.050 --> 21:10.920
They never come back.

21:10.920 --> 21:15.150
Daddy!

22:47.050 --> 22:54.310
<b>SLF Mini</b>

22:47.740 --> 22:51.570
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

22:50.860 --> 22:54.300
<i><b>Pencilgon's
Five-Second Answers</b></i>

22:51.570 --> 22:53.050
Mini!

22:54.310 --> 23:40.350
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

22:57.830 --> 23:04.820
<b>Likes?</b>

22:59.850 --> 23:00.910
Fireworks.

23:01.590 --> 23:04.070
They're beautiful and pure.

23:05.090 --> 23:11.570
<b>Dislikes?</b>

23:06.630 --> 23:07.890
Slugs.

23:07.890 --> 23:11.580
Ugh. I'd like to wipe them 
off the face of the Earth!

23:11.840 --> 23:18.330
<b>What do you think
of Sunraku-san?</b>

23:14.200 --> 23:15.640
He's a freak.

23:16.170 --> 23:18.000
Oh, that's a good thing.

23:18.600 --> 23:26.590
<b>Favorite sayings?</b>

23:21.290 --> 23:22.900
Brains over brawn.

23:22.900 --> 23:24.240
Perfection is real.

23:24.240 --> 23:25.560
Profit while others fight.

23:25.560 --> 23:26.590
And...

23:26.590 --> 23:31.590
<b>What nickname would you give yourself?</b>

23:29.400 --> 23:31.590
"The Perfect Beauty."

23:31.860 --> 23:36.600
<b>What would you compare a Player Killer to?</b>

23:34.750 --> 23:36.600
A runway model, I suppose.

23:36.870 --> 23:47.360
<b>Why is that?</b>

23:38.610 --> 23:40.860
Both inspire cries.

23:40.860 --> 23:42.850
Though the model inspires cries of joy,

23:42.850 --> 23:44.430
while the player killer inspires

23:44.810 --> 23:46.610
death cries!
